==Latin==

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|ine-pro|la}} {{recons|bʰidʰ-|lang=ine-pro}}, [[zero-grade]] of {{etyl|ine-pro|la}} {{recons|bʰeydʰ-||to command, to persuade, to trust|lang=ine-pro}}.
Cognate to Latin {{term|fido|fīdō|I trust|lang=la}} and Proto-Germanic {{recons|bīdaną|lang=gem-pro}}.

====Noun====
{{la-noun|fidēs|fidei|fideī|f|fifth}}

# [[faith]], [[belief]]
# [[reliance]]
# [[confidence]], [[trust]]

